  "backstory": "In the soot-stained labyrinth of Oakhaven’s Lower Ward, the name Willy was a stark contrast to the hulking frame and protruding tusks that marked him as an outsider. Born to the gutter and raised by the indifferent stones of the city, he learned early that his orcish blood was both a curse and a gift. While other children feared the night, Willy’s eyes pierced the gloom with a natural darkvision, turning the lightless sewers into his personal highway. He survived on the periphery of society, a menacing figure whose mere presence silenced the taunts of cruel merchants. His childhood was not one of play, but of endurance; he possessed a relentless spirit that allowed him to rise from beatings that would have broken a common man, his body refusing to fail even when his stomach was hollow with hunger.\n\nWilly did not choose the path of the rogue for the sake of gold, but for the sanctuary of the silence it provided. In a world that looked at his green-tinted skin and saw only a monster, he realized that if he could not be loved, he would be unseen. He refined his natural savagery into a clinical, lethal precision, learning that a well-placed blade from the shadows was far more effective than the clumsy brawling of the docks. His savage attacks were not outbursts of mindless rage, but calculated strikes born of a desperate need to end a fight before it truly began. He became a ghost of the slums, a collector of secrets and a thief of necessities, driven by a burning desire to claw his way out of the filth and prove that he was more than the sum of his scars.\n\nThe call to adventure came when the shadows of the city grew too small for his ambitions. Willy realized that his unique blend of orcish might and street-honed guile could be the key to unlocking the ancient vaults and forgotten ruins that the \"civilized\" folk feared to tread. He seeks now to test his mettle against the greater world, driven by a hidden bond to the orphans he left behind in the gutters and a deep-seated mistrust for those who hide behind titles and coin. He walks the path of the adventurer not to seek redemption for his heritage, but to carve out a destiny where he is the master of his own fate, ensuring that the world will remember the name Willy not as a common urchin, but as a shadow they never saw coming.",
